from common import speaking

WRITING={
7:[dict(prompt="The line graph shows annual visits to public libraries by three age groups in the fictional city of Branton between 2005 and 2025. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant. Write at least 150 words.",visual="![Annual library visits](writing-1.svg)\n\nData (thousands of visits; each visit counted, not unique visitors):\n\n| Year | Under 18 | 18–64 | 65 and over |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| 2005 | 120 | 180 | 60 |\n| 2010 | 135 | 170 | 75 |\n| 2015 | 150 | 145 | 95 |\n| 2020 | 110 | 100 | 90 |\n| 2025 | 160 | 125 | 120 |",guidance="An overview can contrast the net rise for under-18s and over-64s with the net decline for 18–64s. All groups fall between 2015 and 2020, then recover. Under-18 visits overtake 18–64 visits by 2015 and finish highest; the oldest group finishes close to working-age adults. Distinguish visits from unique people. Causes of the 2020 dip are not supplied."),
dict(prompt="Some people think publicly funded scientific research should focus on problems that can be solved soon. Others believe research with uncertain long-term benefits is equally important. Discuss both views and give your own opinion. Give reasons and relevant examples. Write at least 250 words.",guidance="Address near-term public needs and the possible value of uncertain fundamental work. Develop an actual position on priorities or balance. Examples can be hypothetical or drawn from experience; named studies are unnecessary. A balanced position needs a reasoned allocation principle, not merely a final sentence saying both are important.")],
8:[dict(prompt="The charts compare how households in the fictional town of Larton allocated their average monthly expenditure in 2005 and 2025. The totals are given below each chart. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant. Write at least 150 words.",visual="![Household spending shares](writing-1.svg)\n\n| Category | 2005 share | 2025 share |\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\n| Housing | 25% | 35% |\n| Food | 30% | 20% |\n| Transport | 20% | 15% |\n| Leisure | 15% | 20% |\n| Other | 10% | 10% |\n\nAverage total monthly expenditure: 2005, 1,200 currency units; 2025, 2,000 currency units. Figures are nominal; no inflation adjustment is supplied.",guidance="Housing replaces food as the largest share. Housing and leisure shares rise; food and transport fall; other is unchanged as a share. Shares are not amounts: food rises from 360 to 400 units despite falling from 30% to 20%; transport rises from 240 to 300. Other rises from 120 to 200. Do not infer changes in purchasing power from nominal figures."),
dict(prompt="In many cities, workers travel long distances between home and work. What problems can this cause for individuals and communities? What measures could reduce these problems? Give reasons and relevant examples. Write at least 250 words.",guidance="Develop both problems and measures. Individual costs can include time, fatigue and expense; community effects might include congestion or uneven demand. Match proposals to problems and consider practical limits. A response about the benefits of travel alone does not address the task.")],
9:[dict(prompt="The table gives information about three types of visitor accommodation in the fictional region of Penford in 2010 and 2025. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant. Write at least 150 words.",visual="![Accommodation indicators](writing-1.svg)\n\n| Type | Available rooms 2010 | Available rooms 2025 | Average occupancy 2010 | Average occupancy 2025 | Average stay 2010 (nights) | Average stay 2025 (nights) |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| Hotels | 800 | 1,000 | 70% | 68% | 2.5 | 2.8 |\n| Guesthouses | 300 | 250 | 60% | 72% | 3.0 | 3.5 |\n| Self-catering units | 400 | 900 | 55% | 65% | 5.0 | 4.2 |\n\nOccupancy means the average proportion of available rooms occupied, not the share of all visitors.",guidance="Self-catering capacity more than doubles, hotels grow more modestly and guesthouses contract. Guesthouse occupancy rises to the highest rate, while hotels decline slightly. Self-catering stays shorten but remain longest. Do not equate capacity with demand or add occupancy percentages across categories. Select comparisons rather than narrating all 18 values mechanically."),
dict(prompt="Some people believe secondary schools should give students more choice over the subjects they study. Others think all students should follow a broad common curriculum. Discuss both views and give your own opinion. Give reasons and relevant examples. Write at least 250 words.",guidance="Discuss student choice and a common breadth of education. Consider motivation, future uncertainty and access to expertise. The position can favour one view or a justified combination, but should clarify what is compulsory and where choice belongs. Avoid switching to a general discussion of university specialisation.")],
10:[dict(prompt="The diagram shows a proposed industrial process for turning used cork stoppers into floor panels. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant. Write at least 150 words.",visual="![Cork panel process](writing-1.svg)\n\nAccessible diagram transcription:\n\n1. Collect used cork stoppers.\n2. Sort: reject non-cork items (leave the process).\n3. Wash accepted cork.\n4. Dry with warm air.\n5. Grind into granules.\n6. Mix granules with a supplied binder.\n7. Press the mixture into panels using heat and pressure.\n8. Inspect panels: suitable panels go to packing and sale; unsuitable panels are ground again and returned to the mixing stage.\n\nThe binder enters only at mixing. The diagram supplies no times, temperatures or quantities.",guidance="Give an overview of collection, preparation, manufacture and inspection, including the feedback loop. Distinguish rejected non-cork input leaving the process from failed cork panels returning to grinding/mixing. Mention binder input and heat/pressure without inventing numerical conditions. This is an authored proposed process, not a claim about every cork factory."),
dict(prompt="More employers are offering flexible working hours. Do the advantages of this development outweigh the disadvantages? Give reasons and relevant examples. Write at least 250 words.",guidance="Evaluate flexible hours, rather than discussing only home working. Explain benefits and costs for workers or organisations and make a clear comparative judgement. Coordination, service coverage and caring responsibilities are relevant examples. A claim that there are advantages and disadvantages without weighing them leaves the main question unanswered.")],
11:[dict(prompt="The plans show the layout of Market Square in the fictional town of Elwick in 2005 and 2025. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant. Write at least 150 words.",visual="![Market Square plans](writing-1.svg)\n\nThe plans use the same boundaries and orientation (north at the top). Main Road remains along the south edge.\n\n| Position inside square | 2005 | 2025 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Northwest | Car park | Community garden |\n| Northeast | Shops | Shops, same footprint |\n| Centre | Road connecting west and east entrances | Pedestrian path connecting west and east entrances |\n| Southwest | Bus stop | Café with outdoor seating |\n| Southeast | Public toilets | Public toilets, same footprint |\n| North-central | No structure | Covered market pavilion |\n\nIn 2025 the bus stop is on Main Road outside the square, immediately south of its former position. Vehicle entrances at the east and west have become pedestrian entrances. No scale or building dimensions are supplied.",guidance="Overview: the square becomes pedestrian-oriented, with greenery and a pavilion. The car park becomes a garden; the internal bus stop becomes café/seating, with the bus stop moved onto Main Road. Shops and toilets remain; the east–west road becomes a pedestrian path. Avoid claiming all transport is removed from the surrounding area or inferring relative building sizes from an unscaled plan."),
dict(prompt="Some people think communities should organise more activities that bring different age groups together. Others believe separate activities for people of similar ages are more beneficial. Discuss both views and give your own opinion. Give reasons and relevant examples. Write at least 250 words.",guidance="Develop the value of intergenerational contact and of age-specific needs or interests. A combined approach can be argued, with examples of which activities suit each arrangement. Do not assume all members of an age group have identical preferences. State and support the opinion throughout the response.")],
12:[dict(prompt="The bar chart shows the percentage of adults in the fictional region of Norwick who used four methods to learn a new skill in 2015 and 2025. The table gives average weekly study time among users of each method in 2025. Summarise the information by selecting and reporting the main features, and make comparisons where relevant. Write at least 150 words.",visual="![Learning method participation](writing-1.svg)\n\n| Method | Adults using method 2015 | Adults using method 2025 | Hours/week per user 2025 |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| In-person classes | 35% | 30% | 4.5 |\n| Live online classes | 10% | 40% | 3.5 |\n| Recorded courses | 20% | 45% | 2.5 |\n| Printed self-study | 40% | 25% | 3.0 |\n\nRespondents could report more than one method; percentages need not sum to 100. Study time is measured among users, not across all adults.",guidance="Online methods grow strongly; printed self-study and in-person participation fall. Recorded courses become most used, while in-person classes have the greatest weekly hours among users. Live online quadruples its share. Do not sum overlapping respondents, treat hours as total regional hours, or infer that every adult abandons one method for another."),
dict(prompt="People can now publish reviews of products and services immediately online. Is this mainly a positive or a negative development? Give reasons and relevant examples. Write at least 250 words.",guidance="Take a reasoned overall position while acknowledging relevant limitations. Discuss rapid information sharing, accountability or choice alongside credibility, manipulation or unfair judgement. The task concerns the ability to publish immediate reviews, not social media in general. Examples do not need to identify real companies or individuals.")]
}

